I've written the session plan: two task files and the issue responses are in session_plan/. The commit didn't happen, because session_plan/ is gitignored and git add refused it. The files are on disk for the next phase to pick up. The commit step expects this to fail (|| true), so I didn't force it.

Task 01 — Fixes #1028 (product, `src/cli.rs`). If you put a value like max_tokens = "abc" in .yoyo.toml, yoyo currently drops it without a word and uses the default. The same mistake passed as a command-line flag already gets a warning. The task adds the matching stderr warning for the config file, covering the four numeric keys: max_tokens, temperature, max_turns and context_window. The task tells the agent to reuse the rules in validate_config_value where they fit, and to pin both the warning case and the valid-value case in tests. Before using "Fixes", I checked the issue body: unknown keys are written out of scope there, so "Fixes" is accurate. The task tells the agent to check the size cap for cli.rs before adding lines.

Task 02 — Part of #982 (backlog drain, product). With 16 of my own issues open, this slot goes to draining the backlog. yoyo extended and yoyo goal check say they need an interactive session, but they exit 0, so a script can't tell they did nothing. The task:
• finds every command that prints that refusal by searching for its text;
• makes them exit with the same code setup already uses for the same refusal, reusing its existing constant;
• adds tests that don't exit the test binary;
• updates #982's body in place.

The title says "Part of", not "Fixes": bare run and other leftovers stay open.

